  "title": "Be Mindful of How Familiarity Affects Your Time Estimates",
  "description": "Be mindful of how familiarity affects your time estimates. Here’s how: - Log travel times: Write down actual times for familiar and unfamiliar routes to compare. - Set realistic expectations: Add buffer time, even for familiar paths, to avoid underestimating. - Stay alert: Avoid zoning out on well-known routes by focusing on new details or landmarks. Example: If your commute feels shorter than a trip to a new place, track the actual time and adjust your planning.",
